3. Software Developer – ICAR Annual Performance Appraisal Report (APAR) - Responsibilities included form creation, report generation, approval cycle implementation, and monitoring at the reporting and reviewing officer levels. Data was fetched from Web APIs (developed by the team) and displayed in the scientist login, then saved to the database after modifications in modules such as projects, technology, capacity building, awards, etc. PDF generation after final submission was performed by scientists. The same process was later integrated into SPARROW (e-Office) to fetch ARMS (scientist) data through Web APIs developed by the team and the NIC team. PI: Dr. Anil Rai, ADG, ICT Unit, ICAR.
4. Certificate – Web Application for ICAR – Land Record Management System (LRMS)
Developed for ICAR Institutes (Product). Team: Dr. Shashi Bhushan Lal (Lead Developer), Dr. Krishan Kumar Chaturvedi, Dr. Mukesh Kumar, and Avanaksh Singh Sambyal (Associate Developers). Tasks included form creation and report generation, followed by modifications based on changing requirements. Implemented login through Lightweight Directory Access Protocol (LDAP), dashboard, notifications, alerts, email functionality, and data fetching from KRISHI JSON APIs via URLs, which were later saved in the database (as guided by the PI and Reporting Officer). PI: Dr. Krishan Kumar Chaturvedi Reporting Officer: Dr. Shashi Bhushan Lal
5. Project Manager – Academic Management System (AMS) Indian Veterinary Research
Institute (IVRI), Izzatnagar, Bareilly, Uttar Pradesh (an IVRI-sponsored project). Also responsible for development of mobile applications (bilingual and multilingual), app management, analytics monitoring in Firebase Developer Console, issue resolution in Google Play Console, user feedback handling, and uploading new apps or updates (as guided by PI, CCPI, and Co-PIs).
In AMS-IVRI, handled implementation and commissioning of the Academic Management
System in the institute, report creation, and modification of functionalities at each user level. Various modules and functionalities were added, developed, integrated, tested, and commissioned into production within stipulated timelines. AMS is an ICAR-IASRI product approved by DG, ICAR, and is running across 55 universities/institutes in the ICAR domain. Provided technical support (offline and online) during training programs at multiple institutes/universities, including NDRI Karnal, CAU Imphal, BAU Sabour, BAU Ranchi, UHS Dharwad, UHS Bagalkot, UAS Bengaluru, GB Pant Nagar, CSHPK Palampur, AMS Raichur, etc. AMS PI: Dr. Sudeep Marwaha Co-PIs: Dr. Alka Arora, Dr. Soumen Pal, Dr. Mukesh Kumar. Mobile Apps PIs: Dr. Rupasi Tiwari (IVRI), Dr. Triveni Dutt (Former JD(Edu.), IVRI; presently Acting Director, IVRI), Dr. Yashpal Singh (Consultant, IVRI), Dr. J. K. Prasad (Nodal Officer). Web APIs Developed: ICAR-IIMS Portal App, ICAR-Student Portal App, Krishi Kalyan Report for ICAR-KVK Mobile App, IVRI-Artificial Insemination App, IVRI-Extension Methods Tutorial Quiz App, ICAR-AMS Online Examination App (PGS IARI Delhi, AMS NDRI Karnal, AMS RPCAU Samastipur, Bihar). Award: Innovation Year Award by the Vice-Chancellor, UHS Bagalkot, Bengaluru. Team: Dr. Sudeep Marwaha (PI), Manish Chauhan, Dinesh Kumar Rajpoot, Shyam Kumar Chauhan, and Avanaksh Singh Sambyal.
ICAR-IASRI & ICAR-IVRI Mobile Applications - Apps including Animal Reproduction App, Artificial Insemination App, Pig Farming App, Landly Pig App, Dairy Manager App, and Pig Ration App were launched by the Hon’ble Minister of Agriculture / Director General, ICAR at the NASC Complex, New Delhi. Eight ICAR-IASRI & ICAR-IVRI apps were also listed in ICAR-IASRI Hindi magazines/journals and on the IASRI website, including Animal Reproduction App and Pig Farming App.
