10. Self-Developed Mobile Application/Web Apps/Agentic AI Apps or Products
i. PopCens App – A mobile application developed to store census-related data of the population of India. The app supports government policy formulation for different communities across states and UTs. Two versions were developed:
1. Offline data storage in the database.
2. Offline and online storage of data along with PDF generation through the mobile application.
ii. Science Agent using Google’s Agent Development Kit – This project involves the development of an autonomous translation agent designed to translate highly technical and scientific text—spanning physics, chemistry, mathematics, biology, and quantum and allied branches—into local regional languages with zero hallucinations. Powered by the Gemini API and deployed across Google Cloud infrastructure, this foundation-model-driven architecture ensures rigorous factual grounding and contextual accuracy. The translation ecosystem scaled rapidly to ensure global accessibility: it initially launched with 10 core languages, expanded to 49 languages, and now comprehensively supports 249 worldwide languages along with more than 140 dialectal aliases. Link for science agent video: https://youtube.com/watch?v=apom2rO_Xy8 
iii. Database Agent –  An agent which can fetch and store from multiple database(s) and show results in textbox/area using Gemini API/Cloud in plain html with css design. Link for Database Agent video: https://youtu.be/9lub-jwii_g 
iv. Heat Conduction(2D) – The core objective of this project is to implement and run BEM, FEM, and FDM thermodynamic analyses directly within a plain HTML and CSS web interface. I conceptualized this idea in 2021 while struggling to sleep due to intense daytime and nighttime heat radiating from both the interior and exterior walls of my room. A standard ceiling fan offered no relief, simply circulating the stifling air. While air conditioning is a common fix, it is not a sustainable solution; prolonged exposure to artificial cooling reduces the human body's natural efficiency to cope with extreme heat and high humidity. This realization inspired me to build a lightweight, accessible web tool to simulate and analyze structural heat transfer, aiming to discover better architectural and thermal insulation alternatives. Link for Heat Conduction (2D) video: https://youtu.be/XqnMlep9Nq0
v. School Management System (Migrant Workers)- Developed the school management system for migrant workers in ASP.Net Technology, Tailwind and MSSQL Database. Link for SMS for Migrant Workers video: https://youtu.be/cxptr4a71II  
vi. Bio portal - Surrounded by bioinformatics education at the Bioinformatics Division of IASRI, Delhi, I observed the daily friction that researchers and students experience when manually processing NCBI/PubMed sequence data. To address this, I engineered a deterministic sequence analysis engine in Python that queries NCBI's Entrez E-Utilities API using user accession IDs and email credentials. I subsequently evolved this pipeline into an autonomous agent architecture using the Agentic framework, orchestrating biological tool execution with foundation models and deploying a fully serverless infrastructure. To establish a rigorous biochemical and sequence analysis methodology, I studied core sequence and genome analysis techniques, referencing standard bioinformatics educational resources and tutorials by Ms. Lana Dominković and Mr. Abdul Mansoor Alzohairy. Throughout this learning phase, I mastered specialized industry software, including PyMOL, Jalview, UCSF Chimera, and ExPASy tools. Link for bioportal video: https://youtu.be/jLDmXZMZ-OI 
vii. Attendance Portal – In the attendance portal, in-app purchases are processed through a mobile app built using the RevenueCat SDK, and the app is hosted live on the Amazon Store. Authority Admins can add organizations along with their respective members. Once logged in, a member can mark their biometric morning attendance, cast their vote on a specific topic, issue, or problem, and later mark their biometric evening attendance. Admins can view all records for members under their specific authority within their own login dashboard. Admins can also add new topics where voting is required. Furthermore, within a particular organization or authority, individual members have the permission to add other members. Members can unlock full functionality by purchasing monthly, yearly, or lifetime (Pro) access, though this is optional rather than mandatory. To drive adoption, the platform also supports promotional codes and offers a 7-day free trial for new users. Link for attendance portal video: https://youtube.com/shorts/IgAApPS7evk?si=2JzaO6D3VRLf2H 
Along with projects, I also developed other projects, namely, SIRform (mobile and web), census app (mobile and web), pashu prajnan app (online synced), etc.
